<title>UK: IFC sets 5.04 billion peseta four-tranche bond.</title>
<headline>IFC sets 5.04 billion peseta four-tranche bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following four-tanche matador bond was announced by lead manager Banco Central Hispano.</p>
<p> BORROWER   INTERNATIONAL FINANCE CORP</p>
<p>* * * * *</p>
<p>TRANCHE A</p>
<p> AMT    1.260 BLN PTA COUPON     4.40	MATURITY    09.MAR.01</p>
<p>ISS PRICE  PAR</p>
<p>* * * * *</p>
<p>TRANCHE B</p>
<p> AMT    1.260 BLN PTA COUPON     4.50	MATURITY    12.MAR.01</p>
<p>ISS PRICE  PAR</p>
<p>* * * * *</p>
<p>TRANCHE C</p>
<p> AMT    1.260 BLN PTA COUPON     4.60	MATURITY    13.MAR.01</p>
<p>ISS PRICE  PAR</p>
<p> NOTES	FOR TRANCHES A, B AND C REDEMPTION PRICE IS 88.02</p>
<p>		PCT PLUS 104.167 LINKED TO THE MONTHLY AVERAGE</p>
<p>		INCREASE OF THE IBEX INDEX THROUGHOUT THE LIFE OF</p>
<p>		THE BOND.</p>
<p>* * * * *</p>
<p>TRANCHE D</p>
<p> AMT    1.260 BLN PTA COUPON     4.50	MATURITY    14.MAR.01</p>
<p>ISS PRICE  PAR</p>
<p> NOTES	FOR TRANCHE D REDEMPTION PRICE IS 88.02 PCT, AND</p>
<p>		WILL HAVE AN ADDITIONAL AMOUNT LINKED TO THE ONE</p>
<p>		YEAR LIBOR RATE.</p>
<p>COMMON TERMS:</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 S&amp;P	  AAA	 LISTING     MADRID</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
